    {
      "title": "Gadi Eisenkot reaches out to Netanyahu allies as he strives to form government",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/gadi-eisenkot-netanyahu-allies-form-israel-government",
      "description": "<p>Former military chief says prime minister brought Israel to historic crisis and it is approaching ‘point of no return’</p><p>Israel’s former military chief Gadi Eisenkot started the tough task of forming a government on Sunday, reaching out to Benjamin Netanyahu’s allies as he said the veteran prime minister had brought the country to a historic crisis.</p><p>Eisenkot, 66, the leader of the Yashar party, who has vowed to bridge Israel’s deep polarisation under Netanyahu, formally received a mandate from the president, Isaac Herzog, who gave him 28 days to form a government despite his bloc lacking a clear majority.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/gadi-eisenkot-netanyahu-allies-form-israel-government\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-08T17:53:59"
    },
    {
      "title": "Gadi Eisenkot has a chance to form a new government in Israel",
